{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"landmark landmark","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md","fileName":"Landmark.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Landmark","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 13:11\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Spatial Perception and Navigation]] [[Augmented Reality Navigation]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","Wayfinding","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"landmark landmark","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md","fileName":"Landmark.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Landmark","heading":"Landmark","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A landmark is an easily distinguishable object used to maintain spatial orientation, estimate distance or direction, and build landmark and route knowledge.\n\nA global landmark is visible from much of the environment and supplies broad directional guidance. A local landmark supports decisions at a particular point. Effective landmarks are placed where they can be noticed and are visually distinct in color, texture, lighting, shape, or size.\n\nLandmarks make environments more legible and support [[Wayfinding]], [[Spatial Knowledge]], and the construction of a [[Cognitive Map]].\n\nAn AR navigation system can highlight a physical landmark or attach a decision cue to it, connecting digital route information to a feature the traveler can recognize without the display. Stable real-world referents also help relate egocentric guidance to an exocentric overview.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","Wayfinding","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"landmark landmark","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Landmark.md","fileName":"Landmark.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Landmark","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf]]\n[[augmentedreality_pearson.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Spatial Perception and Navigation","Augmented Reality Navigation","Wayfinding","Spatial Knowledge","Cognitive Map","3duserinterfaces2ande.pdf","augmentedreality_pearson.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}